/** @page about About
  @section doc lds-cpp Documentation

  This library provides low-discrepancy sequence (LDS) generators for quasi-Monte Carlo methods.

  The fundamental building block is the van der Corput sequence in base \f$b\f$:
  @f[
      \phi_b(n) = \sum_{k=0}^{\infty} a_k(n) \, b^{-k-1}
  @f]
  where \f$a_k(n)\f$ are the base-\f$b\f$ digits of \f$n\f$.

  Halton sequences extend this to \f$[0,1]^n\f$ by pairing successive bases and are the basis for
  numeric integration (QMC).

  @section use-cases Mappings and applications

  - LDS on the unit circle \f$S^1\f$: initial guesses for Aberth's root-finding method.
  - LDS on the unit sphere \f$S^2\f$: graphics.
  - Grid points on \f$SO(3)\f$ / \f$S^3\f$ (Hopf coordinates): robotics.
  - LDS on the \f$n\f$-sphere \f$S^n\f$: filter-bank design and MIMO wireless channel models.

  @section design Design notes

  - Digits come from reversing the index's bits (base 2) and from bases of the form \f$2^k-1\f$.
  - The generator methods are `constexpr`, so sequences can be evaluated at compile time. That rules
    out `std::atomic` counters; see the sibling project
    [lds-gen-cpp](https://github.com/luk036/lds-gen-cpp) for the runtime, thread-safe variant.

  See the \ref lds "lds" namespace for the full API.
*/
